# THE ISSUES OF `heroes-lang/heroes`, WRITTEN AND READ, a second root of the
# harness:
#
#     heroes run tests/harness/issues.hero -- file <draft.md>
#     heroes run tests/harness/issues.hero -- close <number> <closing.md>
#     heroes run tests/harness/issues.hero -- comment <number> <text.md>
#     heroes run tests/harness/issues.hero -- edit <number> <draft.md>
#     heroes run tests/harness/issues.hero -- open [--kind <k>] [--milestone M-<name>] [--class <c>] [--json]
#
# from the repository's root, always. **Since the author's seven answers of
# 2026-10-12 the issues live on GitHub alone** (the decision
# https://github.com/heroes-lang/heroes/issues/2027,
# filed after the transcription), and these five words are how a session
# writes and reads them; opening, commenting on, closing and correcting an
# issue through them is asked once, by that answer (CLAUDE.md § Hard stops),
# so they take no `--yes`, and no hook sees a write a program `gh` is spawned
# from makes (the last bullet of layer 1 in `.claude/rules/verification.md` §
# A suite is the last judge): the guard is what each refuses before any write.
#
# - `file` opens the issue of a draft a lane wrote outside the tree in the
#   card's shape (`issue_draft.hero`, `issue_write.filed`): refused, with every
#   reason, where the card reader or the rendering rule refuses it, where
#   GitHub lacks a milestone or a label it names, or where its card's `filed`
#   is not the day GitHub dates it; then `POST /repos/heroes-lang/heroes/issues`,
#   the address printed on stdout the moment the issue exists, a defect's title
#   numbered `Defect <number>: ` by its own issue, a decision taken (its item
#   ticked, its card naming the commit that applies it) closed `completed` with
#   its settling comment, and the issue read back; **the draft is removed only
#   once its issue reads back whole** (exit 0), so no copy of an issue stands
#   beside it, and a draft whose run stopped anywhere stays for the rerun,
#   which opens no second issue.
# - `close` appends a closing text to the issue's body under a defect's
#   `## The repair` or every other kind's `## What was done` (the text opening
#   with that heading, or with none, which then takes it), its last line the
#   commit, bare; posts `Fixed by` or `Settled by` and the commit; and closes
#   the issue `completed`.
# - `comment` posts one comment; `edit` makes an OPEN issue's title, body,
#   labels and milestone a corrected draft's, `repair`'s logic for one issue,
#   a closed issue being a record corrected underneath, by `comment`. Each
#   prints the address it wrote.
# - `open` prints the open issues, one line each or JSON (`issue_open.hero`),
#   and writes nothing: the skills' reader of the lists.
#
# **And while `issues/` stands, the transcription's words** (panel 212, the
# files being the truth until the folder goes):
#
#     heroes run tests/harness/issues.hero -- render [--pin <hash>] [<issue file>...]
#     heroes run tests/harness/issues.hero -- plan [--pin <hash>] [<issue file>...]
#     heroes run tests/harness/issues.hero -- push --yes --pin <hash> [--accept-gaps] [<issue file>...]
#     heroes run tests/harness/issues.hero -- repair --yes [--pin <hash>] [<issue file>...]
#     heroes run tests/harness/issues.hero -- prepare --yes
#     heroes run tests/harness/issues.hero -- finish --yes
#
# With no file each takes every issue file under `issues/`; `render` and `plan`
# take any of them, `push` only the first ones whose `github:` is `none`, in
# the cards' order (`filed`, then the name), since each import takes the next
# number GitHub gives, and `repair` those whose `github:` holds an address.
#
# - `render` prints what each issue file becomes on GitHub, one JSON object a
#   line: its path, its milestone and its `Defect` field's numbers (null where
#   it has none), and the payload the import takes. It reads files and asks
#   git; it writes nothing and needs no network. The `Record:` link is pinned
#   at `--pin`, `HEAD` where none is given.
# - `plan` reads GitHub, every request a GET, and writes nothing: what `push`
#   would do (`issue_plan.hero`), then every request it made. Its pin is
#   `--pin`, else the one the run's state records, else `HEAD`.
# - `push` imports the issue files into GitHub (`issue_push.hero`). It is
#   refused without `--yes`, which is its own guard; without a `--pin` that
#   names a commit already on `origin/main` (as this clone last fetched it) and
#   is the one the run's state records, if it records one; and without a
#   `collaborators_only` interaction limit in force, unless `--accept-gaps` is
#   given. Every import is read back, and a body GitHub stored otherwise is
#   told and counted.
# - `repair` makes each issue that differs from its file match it, the file
#   being the truth (`issue_repair.hero`, R10 as the author amended it on
#   2026-10-12): it reads every issue in one list, renders each card at the pin
#   its issue's `Record:` line names (`--pin`, else `HEAD`, where it names
#   none), and writes what differs through the REST route, each issue read
#   back; it runs only with `--yes`.
# - `prepare` performs panel 212's R6 items 3 and 4 before a transcription
#   (`issue_prepare.hero`): the chain's milestones GitHub lacks, the label
#   `kind:learn` deleted, the interaction limit set; `finish` lifts the limit
#   after it. Both write to GitHub, a milestone, a label and an interaction
#   limit staying asked every time (the second answer), so both run only with
#   `--yes`, which `.claude/settings.json` asks the author for.
#
# **What leaves with the folder**: these six words, and the modules they alone
# use, `issue_load.hero`, `issue_plan.hero`, `issue_push.hero`,
# `issue_import.hero`, `issue_state.hero` and `issue_prepare.hero`, with
# `repaired`, `read_all` and `pins_of` of `issue_repair.hero` (whose `owed`
# `edit` keeps). The five words above use none of them.
#
# Panel 212's R1, ratified 2026-10-11, made this a program of the harness and no
# verb of `heroes`, the author reading a Heroes program run with `heroes run` as
# no script (CLAUDE.md § 10); `.claude/rules/records.md` § The issues is the
# rule it renders and writes by. Every request to GitHub goes through `gh`
# (`issue_wire.hero`), which holds the token; this program never reads it.
#
# Exit (R11): 0 clean; 1 the input has diagnostics: a draft or a closing text
# refused, a card that cannot render, a file the pin's tree does not hold, a
# milestone or a label a write names and GitHub lacks, or an issue GitHub still
# holds otherwise after a write, each told on stderr;
# 2 the program could not run: an argument it does not take, a refusal of a
# guard, git or `gh` that could not answer, or a request GitHub refused that
# waiting does not answer.

use cards
use issue_args
use issue_draft
use issue_git
use issue_github
use issue_import
use issue_json
use issue_load
use issue_match
use issue_open
use issue_pace
use issue_plan
use issue_prepare
use issue_push
use issue_repair
use issue_safe
use issue_state
use issue_wire
use issue_write
use records_github
use shell
use strings

extern "hero_os.h"
    function hero_write_err(text: str)

constant SCRATCH: str
    "build/issues"

constant TRUNK: str
    "origin/main"

function main()
    given = args()

    if given.len() == 0 || !issue_args.among(word: given[0], words: issue_args.WORDS)
        told(issue_args.refusal(given))
        exit(code: 2)
    asked = issue_args.parsed(word: given[0], words: given.slice(from: 1, to: given.len()))

    if asked.wrong != ""
        told(asked.wrong)
        exit(code: 2)
    scratch = SCRATCH + "-" + shell.pid().to_str()
    code: i64 @= 0

    if asked.word == "render"
        code @ rendered(scratch: scratch, asked: asked)
    else if asked.word == "plan"
        code @ planned(scratch: scratch, asked: asked)
    else if asked.word == "push"
        code @ pushed(scratch: scratch, asked: asked)
    else if asked.word == "repair"
        code @ repairing(scratch: scratch, asked: asked)
    else if asked.word == "file" || asked.word == "edit"
        code @ drafting(scratch: scratch, asked: asked)
    else if asked.word == "close" || asked.word == "comment"
        code @ answering(scratch: scratch, asked: asked)
    else if asked.word == "open"
        code @ listing(scratch: scratch, asked: asked)
    else
        code @ prepared_or_finished(scratch: scratch, word: asked.word)
    _ = shell.remove_tree(scratch).is_err()
    exit(code: code)

# `render`: each card's line, or why it cannot be rendered.
function rendered(scratch: str, asked: issue_args.Asked) -> i64
    pin: str @= asked.pin

    if pin == ""
        pin @ "HEAD"
    loaded = issue_load.loaded(scratch: scratch, paths: asked.paths, pin: pin)

    if loaded.is_err()
        told(issue_github_failure(loaded))
        return 2

    for one in loaded.must().refused
        told(one)

    for entry in loaded.must().chosen
        print(issue_json.line(entry.r))

    if loaded.must().refused.len() > 0
        return 1
    return 0

# `plan`: what `push` would do, read from GitHub, and every request it made.
function planned(scratch: str, asked: issue_args.Asked) -> i64
    pin: str @= asked.pin

    if pin == ""
        state = issue_state.read_state(issue_state.PATH)

        if state.is_err()
            told(issue_github_failure(state))
            return 2
        pin @ state.must().pin

    if pin == ""
        pin @ "HEAD"
    got = issue_load.loaded(scratch: scratch, paths: asked.paths, pin: pin)
    roadmap = read_file("docs/ROADMAP.md")

    if got.is_err() || roadmap.is_err()
        told(issue_github_failure(got) + issue_github_failure(roadmap))
        return 2
    loaded = got.must()
    refused = judged(scratch: scratch, loaded: loaded)

    if refused < 0
        return 2
    missing = refused - loaded.unrendered
    trunk = issue_load.on_trunk(scratch: scratch, pin: loaded.pin, trunk: TRUNK)
    chain = issue_plan.chain_of(roadmap.must())

    if chain.is_err()
        told(issue_github_failure(chain))
        return 2
    rows = chain.must()
    s: issue_pace.Session @= issue_pace.session(
        transport: issue_wire.gh(),
        world: issue_wire.world_at(scratch),
        live: true
    )
    gh = issue_plan.gathered(@s, entries: loaded.chosen, ask_listing: true)

    if gh.is_err()
        told("GitHub could not be read: " + issue_github_failure(gh))
        return 2
    survey = issue_match.surveyed(
        entries: loaded.chosen,
        chosen: loaded.chosen,
        rows: rows,
        gh: gh.must(),
        pin: loaded.pin
    )
    on: str @= "on " + TRUNK + " as this clone last fetched it"

    if trunk.is_err()
        on @ "whose ancestry git could not say: " + issue_github_failure(trunk)
    else if !trunk.must()
        on @ "NOT on " + TRUNK + " as this clone last fetched it, so `push` refuses it"
    print(
        "plan: " + (loaded.chosen.len() + loaded.unrendered).to_str() + " issue files, " + loaded.chosen.len().to_str() + " rendered, " + loaded.unrendered.to_str() + " refused by the rule and " + missing.to_str() + " not in the pin's tree; pinned at " + loaded.pin + ", " + on
    )

    for line in issue_plan.lines_of(survey: survey, chosen: loaded.chosen, rows: rows, gh: gh.must())
        print(line)

    print("requests: " + s.world.requests.len().to_str() + " to GitHub, every one a read")

    for request in s.world.requests
        print("  " + request.method + " " + request.path)

    if refused > 0
        return 1
    return issue_plan.code_of(survey)

# `push`: the guards, then the imports.
function pushed(scratch: str, asked: issue_args.Asked) -> i64
    pin = issue_git.pinned(scratch: scratch, pin: asked.pin)

    if pin.is_err()
        told(issue_github_failure(pin))
        return 2
    trunk = issue_load.on_trunk(scratch: scratch, pin: pin.must(), trunk: TRUNK)

    if trunk.is_err() || !trunk.must()
        told(
            "the pin " + pin.must() + " is not on " + TRUNK + " as this clone last fetched it, and the `Record:` links name a commit already there (R5)" + issue_github_failure(trunk)
        )
        return 2
    got = issue_load.loaded(scratch: scratch, paths: asked.paths, pin: pin.must())

    if got.is_err()
        told(issue_github_failure(got))
        return 2
    loaded = got.must()
    order = issue_load.out_of_order(every: loaded.every, named: asked.paths)

    if order != ""
        told(order)
        return 2
    refused = judged(scratch: scratch, loaded: loaded)

    if refused != 0
        if refused > 0
            told("push imports nothing while a file cannot be rendered or linked, since every later number would move")
            return 1
        return 2

    if shell.mkdir_all("build").is_err()
        told("cannot make build/ for the run's state")
        return 2
    s: issue_pace.Session @= issue_pace.session(
        transport: issue_wire.gh(),
        world: issue_wire.world_at(scratch),
        live: true
    )
    setup = issue_import.Setup(root: ".", state_path: issue_state.PATH, pin: pin.must(), accept_gaps: asked.gaps)
    return issue_push.pushed(@s, chosen: loaded.chosen, setup: setup)

# `prepare` or `finish`, on the real transport (`issue_prepare.run_word`).
function prepared_or_finished(scratch: str, word: str) -> i64
    s: issue_pace.Session @= issue_pace.session(
        transport: issue_wire.gh(),
        world: issue_wire.world_at(scratch),
        live: true
    )
    return issue_prepare.run_word(@s, scratch: scratch, word: word)

# `repair`: every card holding an address, or those named, each rendered at
# the pin its issue's `Record:` line names (`HEAD`, or `--pin`, where it names
# none), and its issue made to match it (`issue_repair.hero`).
function repairing(scratch: str, asked: issue_args.Asked) -> i64
    pin: str @= asked.pin

    if pin == ""
        pin @ "HEAD"
    fallback = issue_git.pinned(scratch: scratch, pin: pin)
    every = issue_load.issue_files(scratch)

    if fallback.is_err() || every.is_err()
        told(issue_github_failure(fallback) + issue_github_failure(every))
        return 2
    named = issue_load.chosen_of(every: every.must(), paths: asked.paths)

    if named.is_err()
        told(issue_github_failure(named))
        return 2
    chosen: [cards.Issue] @= []

    for issue in named.must()
        if issue.card.github != "none"
            chosen @ chosen.push(issue)
        else if asked.paths.len() > 0
            told(issue.path + " holds no `github:` address, so it has no issue to repair")
            return 2

    s: issue_pace.Session @= issue_pace.session(
        transport: issue_wire.gh(),
        world: issue_wire.world_at(scratch),
        live: true
    )
    gh = issue_repair.read_all(@s)

    if gh.is_err()
        told("GitHub could not be read: " + issue_github_failure(gh))
        return 2
    pins = issue_repair.pins_of(chosen: chosen, held: gh.must().held, fallback: fallback.must())
    loaded = issue_load.rendered_by_pin(
        scratch: scratch,
        every: every.must(),
        chosen: chosen,
        pins: pins,
        fallback: fallback.must()
    )

    if loaded.is_err()
        told(issue_github_failure(loaded))
        return 2

    for one in loaded.must().refused
        told(one)

    if loaded.must().unrendered > 0
        return 1
    return issue_repair.repaired(@s, entries: loaded.must().chosen, gh: gh.must())

# A session on the real transport, its lines printed as they are said.
function live(scratch: str) -> issue_pace.Session
    return issue_pace.session(transport: issue_wire.gh(), world: issue_wire.world_at(scratch), live: true)

# `file` and `edit`: the draft read, checked and rendered (`issue_draft`), and
# its issue opened or made to match it (`issue_write`). An old defect `edit`
# corrects keeps the number its title holds.
function drafting(scratch: str, asked: issue_args.Asked) -> i64
    walked = shell.project_files(scratch)

    if walked.is_err()
        told("git could not say which files the tree holds: " + issue_github_failure(walked))
        return 2
    known: {str: bool} @= {}

    for path in walked.must()
        known[path] @ true

    roadmap = read_file("docs/ROADMAP.md")
    chain: {str: bool}? @= fail(code: "unread", msg: "docs/ROADMAP.md cannot be read")

    if !roadmap.is_err()
        chain @ cards.chain_states(roadmap.must())

    if chain.is_err()
        told("the chain a draft's milestone is held to cannot be read: " + issue_github_failure(chain))
        return 2
    s: issue_pace.Session @= live(scratch)
    numbered: str @= ""

    if asked.word == "edit"
        held = issue_github.issue(@s, number: asked.number)

        if held.is_err()
            told("GitHub could not be read: " + issue_github_failure(held))
            return 2
        old: [str] @= []

        for n in records_github.title_numbers(held.must().title)
            if n <= records_github.OLD_LAST && n != asked.number
                old @ old.push(records_github.padded(n))

        numbered @ old.join(" ")
    path = asked.paths[0]
    draft = issue_draft.drafted(scratch: scratch, path: path, known: known, chain: chain.must(), numbered: numbered)

    if draft.is_err()
        told(issue_github_failure(draft))
        return 2

    if asked.word == "edit"
        return issue_write.edited(@s, number: asked.number, draft: draft.must())
    code = issue_write.filed(@s, draft: draft.must())

    # Its issue read back whole, the draft goes, so no copy of an issue stands
    # beside it; one the program cannot remove is told, the issue standing.
    if code == 0
        if shell.is_directory(path) || shell.remove_tree(path).is_err()
            told("the issue stands, read back whole, and its draft " + path + " could not be removed: remove it")
        else
            told("removed the draft " + path)
    return code

# `close` and `comment`: the text read, the commits it names asked of git, and
# the issue written (`issue_write`).
function answering(scratch: str, asked: issue_args.Asked) -> i64
    text = read_file(asked.paths[0])

    if text.is_err()
        told("cannot read " + asked.paths[0])
        return 2
    words: [str] @= issue_safe.hash_words(text.must())

    for row in strings.lines(text.must())
        if cards.is_full_hash(strings.trimmed(row))
            words @ words.push(strings.trimmed(row))

    commits = issue_git.commits_among(scratch: scratch, words: words)

    if commits.is_err()
        told("git could not say which words name a commit: " + issue_github_failure(commits))
        return 2
    s: issue_pace.Session @= live(scratch)

    if asked.word == "close"
        return issue_write.closed_with(@s, number: asked.number, given: text.must(), commits: commits.must())
    return issue_write.commented(@s, number: asked.number, given: text.must(), commits: commits.must())

# `open`: the open issues GitHub holds, read and printed (`issue_open`).
function listing(scratch: str, asked: issue_args.Asked) -> i64
    s: issue_pace.Session @= live(scratch)
    return issue_open.opened(
        @s,
        wanted: issue_open.Narrowed(kind: asked.kind, milestone: asked.milestone, grade: asked.grade),
        json: asked.json
    )

# The cards `loaded` refused, and those whose file the pin's tree does not
# hold, each told; how many cards, or -1 where git could not say.
function judged(scratch: str, loaded: issue_load.Loaded) -> i64
    for one in loaded.refused
        told(one)

    paths: [str] @= []

    for entry in loaded.chosen
        paths @ paths.push(entry.r.path)

    missing = issue_load.missing_at(scratch: scratch, pin: loaded.pin, paths: paths)

    if missing.is_err()
        told("git could not say which files the pin holds: " + issue_github_failure(missing))
        return -1

    for path in missing.must()
        told(path + ": the pin " + loaded.pin + " does not hold this file, so its `Record:` link would name nothing")

    return loaded.unrendered + missing.must().len()

function issue_github_failure<T>(result: T?) -> str
    return match result
        .ok _  => ""
        .err e => e.msg

function told(text: str)
    hero_write_err(text: "issues: " + text + "\n")
